{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzMm87jHqQEYWcAiZNhFzC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Roadmap — Panel-Ops\n2\t**Owner:** Architect AI. This file is the authoritative execution plan.\n3\t**Read-only for executors and the dashboard.** Runtime status lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\n4\tBaseline statuses here are descriptive only.\n5\t\n6\tExecutor rules (binding for every ticket): read `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl` first, human\n7\tcomments are binding; implement only the assigned ticket; respect invariants; run\n8\tverification; update `roadmap-status.md`; append completion/blockage comment; never edit\n9\t`roadmap.md`; never touch files outside \"Files allowed to change\".\n10\t\n11\tGlobal invariants (apply to every APP/INF/INT ticket): server-side role enforcement;\n12\tsoft deletes only; append-only Activity; all writes via LockService path; no credentials\n13\tin code; Spanish UI text, English identifiers; schemas exactly per `data-model.md`.\n14\t\n15\tPhases: 0 Discovery · 1 Governance + Operational Control · 2 Parts + Quotation ·\n16\t3 Approval + Payment · 4 Optimizer Exports · 5 AI (not yet ticketed).\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Phase 0 — Discovery (human tasks, tracked as tickets)\n21\t\n22\t## DIS-001 — Optimizer Format Samples\n23\t\n24\t- Status baseline: pending\n25\t- Recommended model: human (Management/Advisor) — not an agent task\n26\t- Dependencies: none\n27\t- Objective: Obtain real import files accepted by LEPTON and KDT Optimizer plus full format specs.\n28\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §1–2`. INT-001/INT-002 are hard-blocked on this.\n29\t- Scope: real LEPTON file; real KDT file; exact columns and order; units; decimal separator; delimiter; encoding; grain/rotation rules; material/thickness encoding; edge-band encoding; required vs optional columns.\n30\t- Out of scope: building adapters.\n31\t- Architectural invariants: executors must never invent these formats.\n32\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/optimizers/` (new samples + notes)\n33\t- Deliverables: sample files + `discovery/optimizers/format-notes.md`\n34\t- Verification commands: n/a (human)\n35\t- Acceptance criteria: both files verified accepted by the real software; every format question in `integration-contracts.md` answered in writing.\n36\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n37\t- Architect notes: photograph/screenshot software import screens if docs unavailable.\n38\t\n39\t## DIS-002 — Existing Web Quotation Tool Discovery\n40\t\n41\t- Status baseline: pending\n42\t- Recommended model: human + claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (summarization only)\n43\t- Dependencies: none\n44\t- Objective: Document the current quotation tool: capabilities, restrictions (min part size, face orientation), data outputs, integration options.\n45\t- Context: Route D intake; its validation rules must fold into the canonical validation layer, not be duplicated.\n46\t- Scope: screenshots or technical access; list of operational restrictions; export formats it produces.\n47\t- Out of scope: integration implementation.\n48\t- Architectural invariants: none beyond documentation accuracy.\n49\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/quotation-tool/`\n50\t- Deliverables: `discovery/quotation-tool/notes.md`\n51\t- Verification commands: n/a\n52\t- Acceptance criteria: restriction list complete enough to specify canonical validation rules; integration feasibility stated.\n53\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n54\t- Architect notes: unblocks future Route D ticket; not blocking Phases 1–3.\n55\t\n56\t## DIS-003 — Commercial Inputs Package\n57\t\n58\t- Status baseline: pending\n59\t- Recommended model: human (Management + accountant)\n60\t- Dependencies: none\n61\t- Objective: Collect real commercial inputs: current price tables (panels, cuts by thickness, edge tape/application), customer-supplied-material surcharge rule, current quotation sample, panel-reference catalog, tape types/sizes, transport rules, accountant-validated VAT + withholding treatment, logo + legal company data, delivery terms, avg tickets/day and parts/ticket.\n62\t- Context: master doc §24. Pricing engine (APP-009) configurable but needs real seeds; PDF (APP-010) needs branding/legal.\n63\t- Scope: data collection only.\n64\t- Out of scope: entering data into the system (done via APP-008 UI later).\n65\t- Architectural invariants: never hard-code tax rules; withholding stays configurable until accountant signs off.\n66\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/commercial/`\n67\t- Deliverables: price spreadsheets, quotation sample, catalog list, tax memo, branding assets.\n68\t- Verification commands: n/a\n69\t- Acceptance criteria: APP-008/009/010 can be seeded without inventing any value.\n70\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n71\t- Architect notes: partial delivery acceptable; missing items become explicit blockers on dependent tickets.\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## Phase 1 — Governance + Operational Control\n76\t\n77\t## GOV-001 — Local Roadmap Execution Dashboard\n78\t\n79\t- Status baseline: pending\n80\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n81\t- Dependencies: none\n82\t- Objective: Localhost-only dashboard that reads this `roadmap.md`, shows Kanban of tickets (To Do / In Progress / Blocked / Completed), safely launches approved executor agents, and writes all runtime evidence outside the roadmap.\n83\t- Context: ADR-003. Full normative spec: `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` + master doc §27 (both binding).\n84\t- Scope: exactly two source files `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` and `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`; runtime artifacts `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/`, `comments/`. Cards show ID, title, short description, dependencies + their completion, recommended model, runtime state. Execute button validates: ticket pending, no active run for ticket, dependencies complete (from ledger, not roadmap text), model/runner allowlisted, ticket still exists in roadmap. Claude runner: `claude --model <id> -p \"<ticket-prompt>\" --output-format stream-json --verbose` with exact IDs `claude-fable-5`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-sonnet-5`. Codex is a separate adapter — if unconfigured, mark blocked with clear message, never pass to `claude --model`. Generated executor prompt enforces the executor rules at the top of this file. Logs to `logs/<ticket>-<timestamp>.log`, viewable from card. Comments `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl`, one JSON object per line (`timestamp, author, type: note|completion|blocked, message`), read before execution. Auto-refresh every few seconds. Listen on `127.0.0.1` only. Startup: `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`.\n85\t- Out of scope: authentication, multi-user, remote access, editing roadmap, product code.\n86\t- Architectural invariants: Node 18+; zero external dependencies; spawn with argument arrays, no shell interpolation of client input; explicit model/runner allowlist; ticket-ID validation + path-traversal prevention; one active run per ticket; atomic ledger writes; append-only logs; `roadmap.md` byte-for-byte untouched; history preserved; clear HTTP errors on invalid transitions.\n87\t- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/**`, `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/**`, `comments/**`\n88\t- Deliverables: server.mjs, index.html, initialized ledger.\n89\t- Verification commands: `node --check tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`; `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs &` then `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:PORT/api/tickets | head`; `shasum roadmap.md` before/after full UI session (must match); attempt execute on ticket with incomplete deps (expect 4xx); attempt Codex run unconfigured (expect blocked state).\n90\t- Acceptance criteria: the 13 criteria in `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` §Acceptance, all demonstrated in log evidence.\n91\t- Rollback notes: delete `tools/roadmap-dashboard/`; runtime artifacts keep history, do not delete.\n92\t- Architect notes: this ticket gates all other execution; build first.\n93\t\n94\t## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n95\t\n96\t- Status baseline: pending\n97\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n98\t- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n99\t- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n100\t- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Payments, Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Users, Workflow_States, Activity, Documents, Configuration, Loss_Reasons, Imports.\n101\t- Scope: Apps Script setup script (idempotent) that creates tabs + headers; seed Workflow_States (17 states per `workflow-state-machine.md`), Configuration keys (`vat_rate=0.19`, `edge_waste_factor=1.10`, `quotation_validity_hours=48`, `aging_alert_minutes=60`, `transition_matrix` JSON generated from `workflow-state-machine.md`, `sequences`, empty `withholding_rules`, empty `company_legal_info`), Loss_Reasons starter list, 3 Users placeholders (roles management/sales/billing).\n102\t- Out of scope: business logic, UI.\n103\t- Architectural invariants: header names exactly per `data-model.md`; no extra columns; script idempotent (safe re-run).\n104\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/setup/**`\n105\t- Deliverables: setup script + run evidence (tab list + header screenshots or logged dump).\n106\t- Verification commands: script self-check function that reads back all tabs/headers and diffs against embedded schema, logging PASS/FAIL per tab.\n107\t- Acceptance criteria: self-check PASS on all 16 tabs; seeds present; re-run makes no changes.\n108\t- Rollback notes: workbook is new; delete workbook to roll back.\n109\t- Architect notes: keep schema constants in one module for reuse by later tickets.\n110\t\n111\t## INF-002 — Apps Script Web App Skeleton (API + Auth + Data Layer)\n112\t\n113\t- Status baseline: pending\n114\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n115\t- Dependencies: [INF-001]\n116\t- Objective: Deployable Web App: session identity from Google account, role resolution from Users tab, JSON API router, generic table read layer, single locked write path, ID sequence generator, Activity writer.\n117\t- Context: every later module builds on this. ADR-002 write-path rule.\n118\t- Scope: `doGet` serves SPA shell; `doPost` JSON API with action routing; `getSession()` (email→role, reject unknown); `db.read(table, filter)`, `db.insert/update(table, row)` wrapped in LockService with atomic sequence increments; `activity.log(...)`; error envelope `{ok:false, error, allowed?}`; deployment config (execute as user accessing, domain-restricted).\n119\t- Out of scope: any business module, UI beyond an authenticated \"hello + role\" shell.\n120\t- Architectural invariants: role checks server-side; unknown user → 403 page; no physical deletes; writes only via locked path.\n121\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/core/**`, `src/gas/api/**`, `src/ui/shell/**`\n122\t- Deliverables: deployed test Web App URL + module code.\n123\t- Verification commands: test function suite (Apps Script) covering: unknown email rejected; sequence increments atomically under loop; insert+read round-trip per table; Activity row appended on write.\n124\t- Acceptance criteria: all tests logged PASS; shell loads showing user email + role.\n125\t- Rollback notes: undeploy web app.\n126\t- Architect notes: this is the foundation — review carefully before accepting.\n127\t\n128\t## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n129\t\n130\t- Status baseline: pending\n131\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n132\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n133\t- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n134\t- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n135\t- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n136\t- Out of scope: UI upload widgets (APP-002).\n137\t- Architectural invariants: nothing in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` is ever overwritten/deleted; every stored file gets a Documents row.\n138\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/drive/**`\n139\t- Deliverables: module + test evidence.\n140\t- Verification commands: test creating order tree, storing file in each category, attempting overwrite in original_request (expect rejection), verifying Documents rows.\n141\t- Acceptance criteria: tree matches spec exactly; overwrite rejected; rows correct.\n142\t- Rollback notes: test folders under a `_TEST` prefix, deletable.\n143\t- Architect notes: use Drive folder IDs in Documents, not paths.\n144\t\n145\t## APP-001 — Customers Module\n146\t\n147\t- Status baseline: pending\n148\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n149\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n150\t- Objective: Customer CRUD (soft delete) + search, per `data-model.md#Customers`, roles M/S.\n151\t- Context: `permissions-matrix.md`.\n152\t- Scope: API actions create/update/list/search/deactivate; duplicate warning on (`id_type`,`id_number`); UI form + list (Spanish).\n153\t- Out of scope: purchase history, credit fields.\n154\t- Architectural invariants: billing role read-only here; required fields enforced server-side.\n155\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/customers/**`, `src/ui/customers/**`\n156\t- Deliverables: module + UI.\n157\t- Verification commands: API tests: create valid/invalid, duplicate detection, billing-role write rejected.\n158\t- Acceptance criteria: tests PASS; UI usable end-to-end.\n159\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped; remove files.\n160\t- Architect notes: —\n161\t\n162\t## APP-002 — Tickets Module + Intake\n163\t\n164\t- Status baseline: pending\n165\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n166\t- Dependencies: [APP-001, INF-003]\n167\t- Objective: Ticket creation (ID `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN`), intake channel capture, advisor assignment, Drive case file auto-created, original request upload (immutable), ticket read/update per schema.\n168\t- Context: `data-model.md#Tickets`; stage 1 of the journey.\n169\t- Scope: create ticket (state `received`, `last_activity_at`, Activity row); upload original request via INF-003; edit non-workflow fields (notes, priority, labels, next_action, waiting_on); list with filters.\n170\t- Out of scope: state transitions (APP-003), parts, quotations.\n171\t- Architectural invariants: ticket always has customer, channel, advisor; original request immutable; monthly sequence atomic.\n172\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/tickets/**`, `src/ui/tickets/**`\n173\t- Deliverables: module + intake UI.\n174\t- Verification commands: tests: ID format/sequence across month boundary; folder created; original upload locked; Activity rows.\n175\t- Acceptance criteria: create→view→edit cycle works; invariants verified.\n176\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n177\t- Architect notes: month boundary sequence test is mandatory.\n178\t\n179\t## APP-003 — Workflow State Machine Engine\n180\t\n181\t- Status baseline: pending\n182\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n183\t- Dependencies: [APP-002]\n184\t- Objective: Server-enforced transitions per `workflow-state-machine.md`: matrix from Configuration, role checks, guards, Activity logging, clear invalid-transition errors listing allowed targets.\n185\t- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` is normative including all 8 guards.\n186\t- Scope: `workflow.transition(ticketId, toState, meta)`; guard framework (evidence checks, role checks, quotation/payment prerequisites as pluggable predicates — predicates for not-yet-built modules return \"guard dependency missing\" and block); `lost` from any non-terminal with mandatory reason; M reopen exception.\n187\t- Out of scope: UI (APP-004), quotation/payment guard internals (wired later by APP-009/APP-012 tickets).\n188\t- Architectural invariants: no state change outside this engine; every change → Activity; matrix read from Configuration (versioned), not hard-coded.\n189\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/workflow/**`\n190\t- Deliverables: engine + guard registry.\n191\t- Verification commands: matrix test sweep: every (from,to,role) combination asserted allow/deny exactly per doc; guard failure messages verified.\n192\t- Acceptance criteria: sweep PASS 100%; invalid transition error lists allowed targets.\n193\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n194\t- Architect notes: highest-risk correctness module; architect will review sweep output line by line.\n195\t\n196\t## APP-004 — Kanban, Ticket List, Ticket Detail UI\n197\t\n198\t- Status baseline: pending\n199\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n200\t- Dependencies: [APP-003]\n201\t- Objective: Kanban board (17 states, drag or button transitions via APP-003), ticket list with filters/search, ticket detail with tabs (Summary, Customer, Original request, Parts placeholder, Confirmation, Quotation placeholder, Payment placeholder, Production placeholder, Documents, Activity).\n202\t- Context: master doc §14.2–14.3; card fields per `workflow-state-machine.md` aging section.\n203\t- Scope: card shows ID, customer, #parts, material, value (per role), state, owner, time-in-state, next action, labels, alert dot; role-based value visibility; Spanish UI.\n204\t- Out of scope: parts editor, quotation, payment UIs (placeholders only).\n205\t- Architectural invariants: UI never mutates state directly — API only; value fields hidden from billing except approved tickets.\n206\t- Files allowed to change: `src/ui/kanban/**`, `src/ui/ticket-detail/**`, `src/gas/api/**` (read endpoints only)\n207\t- Deliverables: three views wired to live data.\n208\t- Verification commands: walkthrough evidence: move ticket through received→review→awaiting_confirmation legally; attempt illegal move (UI shows server error).\n209\t- Acceptance criteria: all card fields render; illegal transitions blocked with clear message.\n210\t- Rollback notes: UI-scoped.\n211\t- Architect notes: keep it minimal-click; adoption risk R-09.\n212\t\n213\t## APP-005 — Activity Feed, Aging Alerts, Home Dashboard\n214\t\n215\t- Status baseline: pending\n216\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n217\t- Dependencies: [APP-004]\n218\t- Objective: Home dashboard (new requests, internal >1h tickets, quotations to prepare/awaiting, payments to verify, ready-for-production, daily sales, avg first-response, alerts) + time-driven trigger computing aging per rule (internal vs customer waiting).\n219\t- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` aging rule; master doc §14.1.\n220\t- Scope: trigger every 10 min: flag tickets `aging_critical AND waiting_on=internal AND idle>60min`, write Activity alert (once per breach), severity escalation; dashboard tiles + drill-down.\n221\t- Out of scope: email/WhatsApp notifications (future).\n222\t- Architectural invariants: alerts distinguish internal vs customer wait; trigger idempotent (no duplicate alerts).\n223\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/alerts/**`, `src/ui/home/**`\n224\t- Deliverables: trigger + dashboard.\n225\t- Verification commands: simulate idle ticket (backdate `last_activity_at`), run trigger twice, assert single alert; dashboard tile counts match table queries.\n226\t- Acceptance criteria: Gate 1→2 checklist ready: 10 real orders trackable end-to-end without paper.\n227\t- Rollback notes: remove trigger + UI.\n228\t- Architect notes: closes Phase 1. Gate review before Phase 2 build.\n229\t\n230\t---\n231\t\n232\t## Phase 2 — Structured Parts + Quotation\n233\t\n234\t## APP-006 — Canonical Part-List Editor\n235\t\n236\t- Status baseline: pending\n237\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n238\t- Dependencies: [APP-004]\n239\t- Objective: Parts tab in ticket detail: add/duplicate/edit rows, paste tabular data, per-edge banding, grain, validation per `data-model.md#Parts`, group by material, customer-confirmed / advisor-validated flags.\n240\t- Context: master doc §14.4; stage 3 normalization.\n241\t- Scope: grid UI; server validation (required fields, positive numbers, catalog values); `validation_warnings` surfaced inline; mm-only entry with converter helper; confirmation gate data for guard #1.\n242\t- Out of scope: file import (APP-007), exports.\n243\t- Architectural invariants: parts locked once ticket paid (server); every save validates server-side.\n244\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/parts/**`, `src/ui/parts/**`\n245\t- Deliverables: editor wired into ticket detail.\n246\t- Verification commands: validation matrix tests (each rule violated once); paid-lock rejection test (mock paid state).\n247\t- Acceptance criteria: advisor can normalize a real handwritten list in editor; guards feed state machine.\n248\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n249\t- Architect notes: incorporate quotation-tool restrictions here if DIS-002 delivered; else leave TODO markers referencing DIS-002.\n250\t\n251\t## APP-007 — CSV/XLSX Import + Column Mapping\n252\t\n253\t- Status baseline: pending\n254\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n255\t- Dependencies: [APP-006]\n256\t- Objective: Route B intake: upload file → mapping UI → validation report → apply as Parts draft; Imports row with `mapping_json` reusable.\n257\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §5`.\n258\t- Scope: CSV parse (delimiter/encoding detection with manual override); XLSX via Drive conversion; unit conversion to mm with provenance; per-row error report; nothing applied until advisor confirms.\n259\t- Out of scope: OCR, photos, AI extraction.\n260\t- Architectural invariants: original file stored immutable first; draft-then-apply, never direct write.\n261\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/imports/**`, `src/ui/imports/**`\n262\t- Deliverables: import flow end-to-end.\n263\t- Verification commands: fixture files (clean, messy units, broken rows) → expected ok/failed counts asserted.\n264\t- Acceptance criteria: real customer Excel imported by advisor without developer help.\n265\t- Rollback notes: discard-draft path built in.\n266\t- Architect notes: —\n267\t\n268\t## APP-008 — Price Administration\n269\t\n270\t- Status baseline: pending\n271\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n272\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n273\t- Objective: M-only UI for Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices: new effective-dated rows, activate/deactivate, history view, daily spreadsheet import, config panel (VAT, waste factor, transport, cut rules).\n274\t- Context: `data-model.md` price tables; R-02.\n275\t- Scope: price CRUD (append-only versioning), import mapping for daily price sheet, \"unpaid quotations affected by price change\" report.\n276\t- Out of scope: quotation calculation (APP-009).\n277\t- Architectural invariants: never edit price row in place; M role only; no price in code.\n278\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/prices/**`, `src/ui/prices/**`\n279\t- Deliverables: admin UI + seed from DIS-003 data if available.\n280\t- Verification commands: role tests (S/B rejected); version chain test (update creates new row, old inactive).\n281\t- Acceptance criteria: M updates a price and history is reproducible.\n282\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n283\t- Architect notes: blocked-soft on DIS-003 for real seeds; buildable with placeholder rows flagged `notes=PLACEHOLDER`.\n284\t\n285\t## APP-009 — Quotation Engine + Snapshots + Versioning\n286\t\n287\t- Status baseline: pending\n288\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n289\t- Dependencies: [APP-006, APP-008]\n290\t- Objective: Build quotation versions from parts + active prices: panels, cuts by thickness, customer-supplied surcharge, edge metres ×1.10 waste (requested/waste/billable stored separately), tape + application, transport, adjustments (M-authorized), subtotal, VAT from config, informational withholding, total; full `price_snapshot_json`; 48h validity; versions supersede.\n291\t- Context: master doc §11; guards #2–#3.\n292\t- Scope: calculation service + quotation tab UI; expiry job marks `expired` + label; M validity extension.\n293\t- Out of scope: PDF (APP-010), approval recording (APP-011).\n294\t- Architectural invariants: every version snapshot-complete and reproducible offline; no hard-coded rates; unknown formulas configurable, empty until DIS-003 validates.\n295\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/quotations/**`, `src/ui/quotations/**`\n296\t- Deliverables: engine + UI + expiry trigger.\n297\t- Verification commands: golden-file tests: fixture parts + fixture prices → expected line items and totals (hand-computed); snapshot reproducibility test (recompute from snapshot equals stored totals); waste-rule test (10.0m requested → 11.0m billable).\n298\t- Acceptance criteria: Gate 2→3 input: 5 real quotations match manual calculation.\n299\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n300\t- Architect notes: second highest-risk module; architect reviews golden files.\n301\t\n302\t## APP-010 — Quotation PDF + WhatsApp Templates\n303\t\n304\t- Status baseline: pending\n305\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n306\t- Dependencies: [APP-009]\n307\t- Objective: Branded quotation PDF stored to Drive `03_QUOTATION` + Documents row; pre-filled WhatsApp deep links for the 8 templates in `integration-contracts.md §3` (Configuration-editable).\n308\t- Context: stage 5–6.\n309\t- Scope: PDF from quotation version (48h validity printed, legal info from Configuration); wa.me link builder; send-recording (sent_at, ticket → quote_sent via APP-003).\n310\t- Out of scope: WhatsApp API, email.\n311\t- Architectural invariants: PDF renders only snapshot data (never live prices); templates contain no invented legal text.\n312\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/pdf/**`, `src/ui/quotations/**` (send panel), Configuration template keys\n313\t- Deliverables: PDF generation + template panel.\n314\t- Verification commands: generate PDF from fixture quotation; regenerate after price change → identical PDF (snapshot proof).\n315\t- Acceptance criteria: advisor sends real quotation via WhatsApp with one click + manual send.\n316\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n317\t- Architect notes: branding/legal blocked-soft on DIS-003 (placeholder watermark until then).\n318\t\n319\t---\n320\t\n321\t## Phase 3 — Approval, Payment, Commercial Closure\n322\t\n323\t## APP-011 — Customer Decision Recording\n324\t\n325\t- Status baseline: pending\n326\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n327\t- Dependencies: [APP-010]\n328\t- Objective: Record approved/rejected/changes_requested/pending on active quotation version with evidence doc, loss reasons, comment; drive transitions (guard #3); changes_requested → new version flow.\n329\t- Context: stage 6; `data-model.md#Quotations` decision fields.\n330\t- Scope: decision UI in quotation tab; evidence attach (screenshot of WhatsApp approval acceptable per business decision); version supersede chain visible.\n331\t- Out of scope: payment.\n332\t- Architectural invariants: decision only on active non-expired version; evidence required for approved.\n333\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/quotations/**` (decision actions), `src/ui/quotations/**`\n334\t- Deliverables: decision flow.\n335\t- Verification commands: tests: decide on expired version rejected; approve without evidence rejected; supersede chain integrity.\n336\t- Acceptance criteria: full stage-6 cycle on a real order.\n337\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n338\t- Architect notes: —\n339\t\n340\t## APP-012 — Payments Module\n341\t\n342\t- Status baseline: pending\n343\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n344\t- Dependencies: [APP-011]\n345\t- Objective: Payment registration (cash/transfer/card), evidence attachment to `04_PAYMENT`, billing verification view, billing-only confirmation (guard #5), rejection path, partial/unidentified payment labels.\n346\t- Context: stages 7–8; `permissions-matrix.md`; R-14.\n347\t- Scope: register (S/B/M), verify+confirm (B only, server-enforced, `verified_by` from session), Payments rows per schema, ticket payment fields synced, transitions via APP-003.\n348\t- Out of scope: bank integration, invoicing.\n349\t- Architectural invariants: `status=confirmed` writable only by billing role; evidence mandatory for confirm; amounts immutable after confirm.\n350\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/payments/**`, `src/ui/payments/**`\n351\t- Deliverables: payment flow + billing view.\n352\t- Verification commands: role attack tests: M and S attempt confirm (expect reject); confirm without evidence (reject); post-confirm amount edit (reject).\n353\t- Acceptance criteria: real payment verified end-to-end by billing user.\n354\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n355\t- Architect notes: security-sensitive; architect reviews role tests.\n356\t\n357\t## APP-013 — Commercial Lock + Production Handoff\n358\t\n359\t- Status baseline: pending\n360\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n361\t- Dependencies: [APP-012]\n362\t- Objective: On payment confirmed: freeze quotation (`immutable=true`), lock parts edits, auto-transition to `ready_production` (guard #6), generate technical production package (price-free PDF/sheet: order id, parts, materials, dims, grain, edges, tape, notes) to `05_PRODUCTION`; M-authorized exception flow for post-payment changes (Activity-recorded).\n363\t- Context: stages 8–9; invariant §6.5–6.8 in `architecture.md`.\n364\t- Scope: lock enforcement across parts/quotations APIs; package generator (technical whitelist); exception flow UI (M reason required).\n365\t- Out of scope: optimizer file formats (Phase 4), machine queues.\n366\t- Architectural invariants: whitelist not blacklist for technical fields; no commercial data in package; only path into `ready_production`.\n367\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/handoff/**`, lock hooks in parts/quotations modules\n368\t- Deliverables: lock + package + exception flow.\n369\t- Verification commands: attack tests: edit part on paid ticket (reject); package content scan asserts zero price fields; exception flow leaves Activity trail.\n370\t- Acceptance criteria: Gate 3→4: full intake→ready_production on real orders; immutability attack-tested.\n371\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n372\t- Architect notes: —\n373\t\n374\t## APP-014 — Reports & KPIs\n375\t\n376\t- Status baseline: pending\n377\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n378\t- Dependencies: [APP-013]\n379\t- Objective: Metrics per master doc §18: commercial (requests, sent, approved, paid, conversion, values, loss reasons), time (first-response, request→quotation, quotation→payment, per-state, >1h count; internal vs customer wait split), operational (parts, materials, edge-banded, rework, failed imports).\n380\t- Context: Activity table is the time source of truth.\n381\t- Scope: reports view with date filters; per-role visibility (B: payment metrics only).\n382\t- Out of scope: exports to BI tools.\n383\t- Architectural invariants: metrics computed from Activity/state history, not editable fields.\n384\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/reports/**`, `src/ui/reports/**`\n385\t- Deliverables: reports view.\n386\t- Verification commands: fixture history → hand-computed KPI assertions.\n387\t- Acceptance criteria: management reads pipeline + conversion without asking anyone.\n388\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n389\t- Architect notes: closes Phase 3 / MVP core.\n390\t\n391\t---\n392\t\n393\t## Phase 4 — Optimizer Exports\n394\t\n395\t## INT-001 — LEPTON Export Adapter\n396\t\n397\t- Status baseline: pending\n398\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n399\t- Dependencies: [DIS-001, APP-013]\n400\t- Objective: Canonical parts → LEPTON-accepted file per DIS-001 spec; stored to `05_PRODUCTION`; validation report for untranslatable rows.\n401\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §1`. **Hard-blocked until DIS-001 accepted.**\n402\t- Scope: adapter + export button in handoff view; technical whitelist.\n403\t- Out of scope: KDT (INT-002), inbound import.\n404\t- Architectural invariants: no invented format elements; adapter isolated (core untouched).\n405\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/adapters/lepton/**`\n406\t- Deliverables: adapter + round-trip evidence.\n407\t- Verification commands: golden test vs DIS-001 sample; real-software import test by human (evidence in comments).\n408\t- Acceptance criteria: LEPTON accepts a real exported order file.\n409\t- Rollback notes: adapter-scoped.\n410\t- Architect notes: —\n411\t\n412\t## INT-002 — KDT Export Adapter\n413\t\n414\t- Status baseline: pending\n415\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n416\t- Dependencies: [DIS-001, APP-013]\n417\t- Objective: Same as INT-001 for KDT Optimizer. Independent adapter, no shared layout code.\n418\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §2`. **Hard-blocked until DIS-001 accepted.**\n419\t- Scope / Out of scope / Invariants / Verification / Acceptance: mirror INT-001 with KDT spec.\n420\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/adapters/kdt/**`\n421\t- Deliverables: adapter + round-trip evidence.\n422\t- Rollback notes: adapter-scoped.\n423\t- Architect notes: —\n424\t\n425\t---\n426\t\n427\t## Corrective Tickets\n428\t\n429\t## FIX-002 — Claude Runner Blocked by Interactive Permission Sandbox\n430\t\n431\t- Status baseline: pending\n432\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n433\t- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n434\t- Objective: The spawned `claude` executor process cannot write to disk in background/non-interactive dashboard runs — every Write/Edit/mkdir tool call is rejected because no interactive approver exists for the spawned process, and the ticket ends with zero files created, silently reported as \"blocked\" by the dashboard's generic no-terminal-state fallback. Add the correct non-interactive permission flag to the Claude runner spawn so background execution actually works.\n435\t- Context: Found running INF-001 via the dashboard 2026-07-18. Log evidence: `logs/INF-001-2026-07-18T03-30-00-012Z.log`, result event shows `\"result\": \"...every write-type tool call (Write, Edit) is rejected with \\\"you haven't granted it yet\\\"... No files created, no partial state left behind.\"`. Root cause confirmed at `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` line ~398-404: the spawn args for the claude runner are `['--model', model, '-p', prompt, '--output-format', 'stream-json', '--verbose']` — missing a non-interactive permission flag.\n436\t- Scope: Add `--permission-mode acceptEdits` (auto-accept edits within the ticket's declared file scope; do NOT use `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, which also grants unrestricted Bash and is broader than this ticket needs) to the claude spawn args in `launchExecution()`. Confirm the executor prompt built by `buildTicketPrompt()` already constrains file scope via each ticket's \"Files allowed to change\" (it does — no prompt change needed unless testing shows otherwise).\n437\t- Out of scope: Codex runner changes, UI changes, roadmap.md ticket content changes.\n438\t- Architectural invariants: same as GOV-001 — spawn via argument array only (flag is a literal array element, not shell-interpolated); no external deps; roadmap.md untouched.\n439\t- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`, `roadmap-status.md`, `comments/**`, `logs/**`\n440\t- Deliverables: patched server.mjs.\n441\t- Verification commands: re-run INF-001 through the dashboard end-to-end (`POST /api/execute {\"ticket\":\"INF-001\",\"runner\":\"claude\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\"}`); confirm log shows actual Write/Edit tool calls succeeding (not permission rejections); confirm ledger reaches `completed` or a genuine `blocked` (spec-reason, not permission-reason) state; confirm no Bash commands run outside what INF-001's own scope implies (spot-check log for absence of unrelated destructive commands, since acceptEdits still gates Bash separately from Edit/Write).\n442\t- Acceptance criteria: a background-launched ticket can actually write its deliverables without a human clicking approval prompts; INF-001 completes for real (16 Sheets tabs bootstrap script delivered) or fails for a genuine spec/business reason, never for permission-sandbox reasons.\n443\t- Rollback notes: revert the single spawn-args line.\n444\t- Architect notes: this was mistaken for a UI bug (FIX-001 already fixed a real but separate defect); this is a process-spawn config gap. Do not conflate the two in the fix.\n445\t\n446\t## FIX-001 — Execute Button Always Disabled (el() null-attribute bug)\n447\t\n448\t- Status baseline: pending\n449\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n450\t- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n451\t- Objective: Fix UI defect in `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`: the `el()` helper calls `setAttribute(k, v)` for null/undefined/false values; `disabled` is a boolean HTML attribute, so its mere presence disables the element. Result: every Execute button renders disabled (cursor not-allowed) even for eligible tickets like INF-001.\n452\t- Context: Found during architect acceptance follow-up 2026-07-18. Root cause at the `el()` helper (~line 205–215) combined with `disabled: (!canExecute || ticket.hasActiveRun) ? 'true' : null` in the card renderer.\n453\t- Scope: In `el()`, skip setting any attribute whose value is null, undefined, or false. Audit index.html for other attrs relying on the broken behavior.\n454\t- Out of scope: server.mjs, any other feature or styling change.\n455\t- Architectural invariants: same as GOV-001 (roadmap.md untouched; no external deps).\n456\t- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`, `roadmap-status.md`, `comments/**`, `logs/**`\n457\t- Deliverables: patched index.html.\n458\t- Verification commands: reload dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:4570; INF-001 Execute button enabled (clickable); GOV-001 (completed) button still disabled; disabled buttons still show not-allowed cursor.\n459\t- Acceptance criteria: eligible pending ticket executable from UI; completed/active tickets remain non-executable.\n460\t- Rollback notes: single-file revert.\n461\t- Architect notes: one-line class of bug; do not refactor beyond the fix.\n462\t\n463\t---\n464\t\n465\t## Phase 5 — Controlled AI Assistance (not yet ticketed)\n466\t\n467\tOutline only: OCR/photo interpretation, external-format mapping, draft ticket creation,\n468\tclarification suggestions, operational follow-up agent, daily summary. Tickets will be\n469\tspecified only after Gate 4 and a dedicated ADR; AI safeguards per `permissions-matrix.md`\n470\tfinal section are non-negotiable.\n471\t\n472\t---\n473\t\n474\t## Dependency Graph\n475\t\n476\t```mermaid\n477\tflowchart LR\n478\t    GOV001[GOV-001] --> INF001[INF-001] --> INF002[INF-002]\n479\t    INF002 --> INF003[INF-003] & APP001[APP-001] & APP008[APP-008]\n480\t    APP001 --> APP002[APP-002]\n481\t    INF003 --> APP002\n482\t    APP002 --> APP003[APP-003] --> APP004[APP-004] --> APP005[APP-005]\n483\t    APP004 --> APP006[APP-006] --> APP007[APP-007]\n484\t    APP006 --> APP009\n485\t    APP008 --> APP009[APP-009] --> APP010[APP-010] --> APP011[APP-011] --> APP012[APP-012] --> APP013[APP-013] --> APP014[APP-014]\n486\t    DIS001[DIS-001] --> INT001[INT-001] & INT002[INT-002]\n487\t    APP013 --> INT001 & INT002\n488\t    DIS003[DIS-003] -.seeds.-> APP008 & APP009 & APP010\n489\t    DIS002[DIS-002] -.rules.-> APP006\n490\t```\n491\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0826cfc-acca-4e95-9633-d053020c806f","uuid":"9a624592-31bf-48ab-9348-3d0c3ed20f65","timestamp":"2026-07-18T03:44:10.563Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/work945/Documents/Proyectos/ABM/proyectos/panel-ops/roadmap.md","content":"# Roadmap — Panel-Ops\n**Owner:** Architect AI. This file is the authoritative execution plan.\n**Read-only for executors and the dashboard.** Runtime status lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\nBaseline statuses here are descriptive only.\n\nExecutor rules (binding for every ticket): read `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl` first, human\ncomments are binding; implement only the assigned ticket; respect invariants; run\nverification; update `roadmap-status.md`; append completion/blockage comment; never edit\n`roadmap.md`; never touch files outside \"Files allowed to change\".\n\nGlobal invariants (apply to every APP/INF/INT ticket): server-side role enforcement;\nsoft deletes only; append-only Activity; all writes via LockService path; no credentials\nin code; Spanish UI text, English identifiers; schemas exactly per `data-model.md`.\n\nPhases: 0 Discovery · 1 Governance + Operational Control · 2 Parts + Quotation ·\n3 Approval + Payment · 4 Optimizer Exports · 5 AI (not yet ticketed).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0 — Discovery (human tasks, tracked as tickets)\n\n## DIS-001 — Optimizer Format Samples\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: human (Management/Advisor) — not an agent task\n- Dependencies: none\n- Objective: Obtain real import files accepted by LEPTON and KDT Optimizer plus full format specs.\n- Context: `integration-contracts.md §1–2`. INT-001/INT-002 are hard-blocked on this.\n- Scope: real LEPTON file; real KDT file; exact columns and order; units; decimal separator; delimiter; encoding; grain/rotation rules; material/thickness encoding; edge-band encoding; required vs optional columns.\n- Out of scope: building adapters.\n- Architectural invariants: executors must never invent these formats.\n- Files allowed to change: `discovery/optimizers/` (new samples + notes)\n- Deliverables: sample files + `discovery/optimizers/format-notes.md`\n- Verification commands: n/a (human)\n- Acceptance criteria: both files verified accepted by the real software; every format question in `integration-contracts.md` answered in writing.\n- Rollback notes: n/a\n- Architect notes: photograph/screenshot software import screens if docs unavailable.\n\n## DIS-002 — Existing Web Quotation Tool Discovery\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: human + claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (summarization only)\n- Dependencies: none\n- Objective: Document the current quotation tool: capabilities, restrictions (min part size, face orientation), data outputs, integration options.\n- Context: Route D intake; its validation rules must fold into the canonical validation layer, not be duplicated.\n- Scope: screenshots or technical access; list of operational restrictions; export formats it produces.\n- Out of scope: integration implementation.\n- Architectural invariants: none beyond documentation accuracy.\n- Files allowed to change: `discovery/quotation-tool/`\n- Deliverables: `discovery/quotation-tool/notes.md`\n- Verification commands: n/a\n- Acceptance criteria: restriction list complete enough to specify canonical validation rules; integration feasibility stated.\n- Rollback notes: n/a\n- Architect notes: unblocks future Route D ticket; not blocking Phases 1–3.\n\n## DIS-003 — Commercial Inputs Package\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: human (Management + accountant)\n- Dependencies: none\n- Objective: Collect real commercial inputs: current price tables (panels, cuts by thickness, edge tape/application), customer-supplied-material surcharge rule, current quotation sample, panel-reference catalog, tape types/sizes, transport rules, accountant-validated VAT + withholding treatment, logo + legal company data, delivery terms, avg tickets/day and parts/ticket.\n- Context: master doc §24. Pricing engine (APP-009) configurable but needs real seeds; PDF (APP-010) needs branding/legal.\n- Scope: data collection only.\n- Out of scope: entering data into the system (done via APP-008 UI later).\n- Architectural invariants: never hard-code tax rules; withholding stays configurable until accountant signs off.\n- Files allowed to change: `discovery/commercial/`\n- Deliverables: price spreadsheets, quotation sample, catalog list, tax memo, branding assets.\n- Verification commands: n/a\n- Acceptance criteria: APP-008/009/010 can be seeded without inventing any value.\n- Rollback notes: n/a\n- Architect notes: partial delivery acceptable; missing items become explicit blockers on dependent tickets.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Governance + Operational Control\n\n## GOV-001 — Local Roadmap Execution Dashboard\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n- Dependencies: none\n- Objective: Localhost-only dashboard that reads this `roadmap.md`, shows Kanban of tickets (To Do / In Progress / Blocked / Completed), safely launches approved executor agents, and writes all runtime evidence outside the roadmap.\n- Context: ADR-003. Full normative spec: `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` + master doc §27 (both binding).\n- Scope: exactly two source files `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` and `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`; runtime artifacts `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/`, `comments/`. Cards show ID, title, short description, dependencies + their completion, recommended model, runtime state. Execute button validates: ticket pending, no active run for ticket, dependencies complete (from ledger, not roadmap text), model/runner allowlisted, ticket still exists in roadmap. Claude runner: `claude --model <id> -p \"<ticket-prompt>\" --output-format stream-json --verbose` with exact IDs `claude-fable-5`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-sonnet-5`. Codex is a separate adapter — if unconfigured, mark blocked with clear message, never pass to `claude --model`. Generated executor prompt enforces the executor rules at the top of this file. Logs to `logs/<ticket>-<timestamp>.log`, viewable from card. Comments `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl`, one JSON object per line (`timestamp, author, type: note|completion|blocked, message`), read before execution. Auto-refresh every few seconds. Listen on `127.0.0.1` only. Startup: `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`.\n- Out of scope: authentication, multi-user, remote access, editing roadmap, product code.\n- Architectural invariants: Node 18+; zero external dependencies; spawn with argument arrays, no shell interpolation of client input; explicit model/runner allowlist; ticket-ID validation + path-traversal prevention; one active run per ticket; atomic ledger writes; append-only logs; `roadmap.md` byte-for-byte untouched; history preserved; clear HTTP errors on invalid transitions.\n- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/**`, `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/**`, `comments/**`\n- Deliverables: server.mjs, index.html, initialized ledger.\n- Verification commands: `node --check tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`; `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs &` then `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:PORT/api/tickets | head`; `shasum roadmap.md` before/after full UI session (must match); attempt execute on ticket with incomplete deps (expect 4xx); attempt Codex run unconfigured (expect blocked state).\n- Acceptance criteria: the 13 criteria in `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` §Acceptance, all demonstrated in log evidence.\n- Rollback notes: delete `tools/roadmap-dashboard/`; runtime artifacts keep history, do not delete.\n- Architect notes: this ticket gates all other execution; build first.\n\n## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Payments, Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Users, Workflow_States, Activity, Documents, Configuration, Loss_Reasons, Imports.\n- Scope: Apps Script setup script (idempotent) that creates tabs + headers; seed Workflow_States (17 states per `workflow-state-machine.md`), Configuration keys (`vat_rate=0.19`, `edge_waste_factor=1.10`, `quotation_validity_hours=48`, `aging_alert_minutes=60`, `transition_matrix` JSON generated from `workflow-state-machine.md`, `sequences`, empty `withholding_rules`, empty `company_legal_info`), Loss_Reasons starter list, 3 Users placeholders (roles management/sales/billing).\n- Out of scope: business logic, UI.\n- Architectural invariants: header names exactly per `data-model.md`; no extra columns; script idempotent (safe re-run).\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/setup/**`\n- Deliverables: setup script + run evidence (tab list + header screenshots or logged dump).\n- Verification commands: script self-check function that reads back all tabs/headers and diffs against embedded schema, logging PASS/FAIL per tab.\n- Acceptance criteria: self-check PASS on all 16 tabs; seeds present; re-run makes no changes.\n- Rollback notes: workbook is new; delete workbook to roll back.\n- Architect notes: keep schema constants in one module for reuse by later tickets.\n\n## INF-002 — Apps Script Web App Skeleton (API + Auth + Data Layer)\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n- Dependencies: [INF-001]\n- Objective: Deployable Web App: session identity from Google account, role resolution from Users tab, JSON API router, generic table read layer, single locked write path, ID sequence generator, Activity writer.\n- Context: every later module builds on this. ADR-002 write-path rule.\n- Scope: `doGet` serves SPA shell; `doPost` JSON API with action routing; `getSession()` (email→role, reject unknown); `db.read(table, filter)`, `db.insert/update(table, row)` wrapped in LockService with atomic sequence increments; `activity.log(...)`; error envelope `{ok:false, error, allowed?}`; deployment config (execute as user accessing, domain-restricted).\n- Out of scope: any business module, UI beyond an authenticated \"hello + role\" shell.\n- Architectural invariants: role checks server-side; unknown user → 403 page; no physical deletes; writes only via locked path.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/core/**`, `src/gas/api/**`, `src/ui/shell/**`\n- Deliverables: deployed test Web App URL + module code.\n- Verification commands: test function suite (Apps Script) covering: unknown email rejected; sequence increments atomically under loop; insert+read round-trip per table; Activity row appended on write.\n- Acceptance criteria: all tests logged PASS; shell loads showing user email + role.\n- Rollback notes: undeploy web app.\n- Architect notes: this is the foundation — review carefully before accepting.\n\n## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n- Out of scope: UI upload widgets (APP-002).\n- Architectural invariants: nothing in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` is ever overwritten/deleted; every stored file gets a Documents row.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/drive/**`\n- Deliverables: module + test evidence.\n- Verification commands: test creating order tree, storing file in each category, attempting overwrite in original_request (expect rejection), verifying Documents rows.\n- Acceptance criteria: tree matches spec exactly; overwrite rejected; rows correct.\n- Rollback notes: test folders under a `_TEST` prefix, deletable.\n- Architect notes: use Drive folder IDs in Documents, not paths.\n\n## APP-001 — Customers Module\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n- Objective: Customer CRUD (soft delete) + search, per `data-model.md#Customers`, roles M/S.\n- Context: `permissions-matrix.md`.\n- Scope: API actions create/update/list/search/deactivate; duplicate warning on (`id_type`,`id_number`); UI form + list (Spanish).\n- Out of scope: purchase history, credit fields.\n- Architectural invariants: billing role read-only here; required fields enforced server-side.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/customers/**`, `src/ui/customers/**`\n- Deliverables: module + UI.\n- Verification commands: API tests: create valid/invalid, duplicate detection, billing-role write rejected.\n- Acceptance criteria: tests PASS; UI usable end-to-end.\n- Rollback notes: module-scoped; remove files.\n- Architect notes: —\n\n## APP-002 — Tickets Module + Intake\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n- Dependencies: [APP-001, INF-003]\n- Objective: Ticket creation (ID `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN`), intake channel capture, advisor assignment, Drive case file auto-created, original request upload (immutable), ticket read/update per schema.\n- Context: `data-model.md#Tickets`; stage 1 of the journey.\n- Scope: create ticket (state `received`, `last_activity_at`, Activity row); upload original request via INF-003; edit non-workflow fields (notes, priority, labels, next_action, waiting_on); list with filters.\n- Out of scope: state transitions (APP-003), parts, quotations.\n- Architectural invariants: ticket always has customer, channel, advisor; original request immutable; monthly sequence atomic.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/tickets/**`, `src/ui/tickets/**`\n- Deliverables: module + intake UI.\n- Verification commands: tests: ID format/sequence across month boundary; folder created; original upload locked; Activity rows.\n- Acceptance criteria: create→view→edit cycle works; invariants verified.\n- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n- Architect notes: month boundary sequence test is mandatory.\n\n## APP-003 — Workflow State Machine Engine\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n- Dependencies: [APP-002]\n- Objective: Server-enforced transitions per `workflow-state-machine.md`: matrix from Configuration, role checks, guards, Activity logging, clear invalid-transition errors listing allowed targets.\n- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` is normative including all 8 guards.\n- Scope: `workflow.transition(ticketId, toState, meta)`; guard framework (evidence checks, role checks, quotation/payment prerequisites as pluggable predicates — predicates for not-yet-built modules return \"guard dependency missing\" and block); `lost` from any non-terminal with mandatory reason; M reopen exception.\n- Out of scope: UI (APP-004), quotation/payment guard internals (wired later by APP-009/APP-012 tickets).\n- Architectural invariants: no state change outside this engine; every change → Activity; matrix read from Configuration (versioned), not hard-coded.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/workflow/**`\n- Deliverables: engine + guard registry.\n- Verification commands: matrix test sweep: every (from,to,role) combination asserted allow/deny exactly per doc; guard failure messages verified.\n- Acceptance criteria: sweep PASS 100%; invalid transition error lists allowed targets.\n- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n- Architect notes: highest-risk correctness module; architect will review sweep output line by line.\n\n## APP-004 — Kanban, Ticket List, Ticket Detail UI\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n- Dependencies: [APP-003]\n- Objective: Kanban board (17 states, drag or button transitions via APP-003), ticket list with filters/search, ticket detail with tabs (Summary, Customer, Original request, Parts placeholder, Confirmation, Quotation placeholder, Payment placeholder, Production placeholder, Documents, Activity).\n- Context: master doc §14.2–14.3; card fields per `workflow-state-machine.md` aging section.\n- Scope: card shows ID, customer, #parts, material, value (per role), state, owner, time-in-state, next action, labels, alert dot; role-based value visibility; Spanish UI.\n- Out of scope: parts editor, quotation, payment UIs (placeholders only).\n- Architectural invariants: UI never mutates state directly — API only; value fields hidden from billing except approved tickets.\n- Files allowed to change: `src/ui/kanban/**`, `src/ui/ticket-detail/**`, `src/gas/api/**` (read endpoints only)\n- Deliverables: three views wired to live data.\n- Verification commands: walkthrough evidence: move ticket through received→review→awaiting_confirmation legally; attempt illegal move (UI shows server error).\n- Acceptance criteria: all card fields render; illegal transitions blocked with clear message.\n- Rollback notes: UI-scoped.\n- Architect notes: keep it minimal-click; adoption risk R-09.\n\n## APP-005 — Activity Feed, Aging Alerts, Home Dashboard\n\n- Status baseline: pending\n- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n- Dependencies: [APP-004]\n- Objective: Home dashboard (new requests, internal >1h tickets, quotations to prepare/awaiting, payments to verify, ready-for-production, daily sales, avg first-response, alerts) + time-driven trigger computing aging per rule (internal vs customer waiting).\n- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` aging rule; master doc §14.1.\n- Scope: trigger every 10 min: flag tickets `aging_critical AND waiting_on=internal AND idle>60min`, write Activity alert (once per breach), severity escalation; dashboard tiles + drill-down.\n- Out of scope: email/WhatsApp notifications (future).\n- Architectural invariants: alerts distinguish internal vs customer wait; trigger idempotent (no duplicate alerts).\n- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/alerts/**`, `src/ui/home/**`\n- Deliverables: trigger + dashboard.\n- Verification commands: simulate idle ticket (backdate `last_activity_at`), run trigger twice, assert single alert; dashboard tile counts match table queries.\n- Acceptance criteria: Gate 1→2 checklist ready: 10 real orders trackable end-to-end without paper.\n- Rollback notes: remove trigger + UI.\n- Architect notes: closes Phase 1. Gate review before Phase 2 build.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Structured Parts + Quotation\n\n## APP-006 —